            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Judy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this all the time except I add mixed vegetables to the beef part. On days when I’m crunched for time, I have cheated and used Bob Evans mashed potatoes on top. Nobody has ever known the difference. This dish is really great on cold nights.",
            "datePublished": "2024-08-05T20:18:15.234Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KFinn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow. This was delicious! I followed the recipe with two exceptions: I added 1/2 cup frozen peas and 1 teaspoon of Henderson's Relish (a Yorkshire specialty). Cooked everything in a cast iron pan and let it simmer until it was nice and thick, then topped it with mashed potatoes and grated Cabot's Extra Sharp Cheddar. Normally we don't like cinnamon in our beef dishes but after everything simmered the flavors of the seasonings mellowed and it wasn't cinnamony at all, just incredible tasty.",
            "datePublished": "2018-02-18T02:12:46.650Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
